From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 22:20:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 56/87] =?UTF-8?q?rga:=200057=20=E2=80=94=20job=20holds=20a?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20session=20reference=20across=20its=20lifetime?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The async completion path (rga_request_release_signal in the RGA2 IRQ
thread) dereferences job->session (->last_active, ->pname) long after the
submitting ioctl returned. The job cached job->session in rga_job_commit()
with no reference; the owning session's only protection was the *request's*
session reference, which is dropped when the request retires. On owning-fd
close, rga_request_session_destroy_abort() retires the requests and
rga_release() then drops the session's own reference while an async job may
still be executing on hardware — freeing the rga_session under the completing
IRQ thread.

KASAN slab-use-after-free (read of session->tgid at rga_request_release_signal)
reproduced on debug build P70a5 via kernel-drivers/tests/rga-session-uaf.sh
cross once the reproducer allocates below-4G CMA buffers so the small RGBA blit
is assignable to RGA2 and async jobs actually submit.

0052 made the *request* refcount drop idempotent; this is the distinct *job*
vs *session* lifetime. Take an independent rga_session_get() when the job
caches job->session and release it in rga_job_free() (the single terminal free
for both the kref and early-error paths; kzalloc leaves job->session NULL so
the put is NULL-guarded).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_job.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_job.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_job.c
index cc8e9a7bc9655..ec709f5b84d83 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_job.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_job.c
@@ -26,6 +26,14 @@ static void rga_job_free(struct rga_job *job)
 	kfree(job->task_buffers);
 	job->task_buffers = NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * Balance the rga_session_get() taken in rga_job_commit() when the job
+	 * cached job->session. NULL on jobs freed before the session was
+	 * assigned (early rga_job_alloc error paths); kzalloc leaves it NULL.
+	 */
+	if (job->session)
+		rga_session_put(job->session);
+
 	kfree(job);
 }
 
@@ -425,6 +433,17 @@ int rga_job_commit(struct rga_req *task_list, size_t task_count, struct rga_requ
 
 	job->request_id = request->id;
 	job->session = request->session;
+	/*
+	 * The job caches the owning session pointer and dereferences it from
+	 * the async completion path (job->session->last_active / ->pname), which
+	 * runs in the hardware IRQ thread long after the ioctl returns. The
+	 * request's session reference is dropped when the request retires, which
+	 * can happen (on owning-fd close) while this job is still in flight on
+	 * hardware. Hold an independent session reference for the job's lifetime
+	 * so the session cannot be freed under the completing IRQ thread; it is
+	 * released in rga_job_free().
+	 */
+	rga_session_get(request->session);
 	job->mm = request->current_mm;
 
 	scheduler = rga_job_schedule(job);
